### Variables
@proxy = https://localhost:7257
@issuer = {{proxy}}/issuer

### 1. Issuer metadata (OID4VCI Section 11.2.1)
GET {{issuer}}/.well-known/openid-credential-issuer
Accept: application/json

### 2. Authorization server metadata (RFC 8414 + OID4VCI Section 11.2.3)
GET {{issuer}}/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server
Accept: application/json

### 3. Mint a credential offer (admin) — defaults to PractitionerLicenseCredential
POST {{issuer}}/credential-offer
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 3b. Mint with custom subject claims
POST {{issuer}}/credential-offer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "credentialConfigurationId": "PractitionerLicenseCredential",
  "subjectClaims": {
    "practitionerName": "Dr. Alex Park",
    "licenseNumber": "MD-2026-99999",
    "specialty": "Cardiology",
    "jurisdiction": "OR"
  }
}

### 4. Token endpoint — pre-authorized code grant (OID4VCI Section 6)
# Replace @preAuthCode with the value from the offer response above.
@preAuthCode = REPLACE-ME

POST {{issuer}}/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:pre-authorized_code&pre-authorized_code={{preAuthCode}}

### 5. Nonce endpoint (OID4VCI Section 7)
POST {{issuer}}/nonce

### 6. Credential endpoint (OID4VCI Section 8)
# Requires a Bearer access_token from /token AND a proof JWT bound to
# the c_nonce from /nonce. Easiest path: drive the flow from the Holder
# wallet — see TrustCartographer.Holder.http.
@accessToken = REPLACE-ME
@proofJwt = REPLACE-ME

POST {{issuer}}/credential
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "credential_configuration_id": "PractitionerLicenseCredential",
  "proofs": {
    "jwt": ["{{proofJwt}}"]
  }
}

### Diagnostics
GET {{issuer}}/info
GET {{issuer}}/health
